WEBVTT

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.056
about how happy it made them,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.016
how it encouraged them
to be their authentic selves.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.296
And I started to think,

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.896
maybe this is the time to tell that
little voice in my head to just shut up

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.680
and let myself be me.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.616
But then things got a little too big.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.336
Carrie Dragshaw was everywhere --
In the "New York Post", "US Weekly" --

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.656
and I got terrified:

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.216
"What would my bosses think?

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.496
Would my coworkers
still respect me as a leader?

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.096
What would my clients think?"

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.976
I thought I was going to have to
get a different job.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.776
But then, something happened,
something small.